    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.test\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nI am using mini.nvim on a linux machine with an encrypted home directory. In consequence, the filesystem of my home directory is _ecryptfs_.\n\nUnfortunately, ecryptfs has a maximum filename length of 143 characters. When I attempt to `git clone` mini.nvim somewhere in my home directory (as done by the lazy plugin manager), cloning fails with the error message \"filename too long\".\n\nThis is apparently due to some of the tests in the path `mini.nvim/tests/screenshots/` having long filenames. One example is `tests-test_test.lua---gen_reporter---buffer---test-+-args-{-'\\''window-=-{-width-=-0.9---vim.o.columns,-col-=-0.05---vim.o.columns,-border-=-'\\''double'\\'',-title-=-('\\''a'\\'')-rep(200)-}'\\''-}` (193 chars).\n\nI see that the filename of the test file is not arbitrary and that it has some function. But in order to support using mini.nvim together with ecryptfs, one could consider shortening the filenames of the tests files.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create an encrypted file system on a linux system using ecryptfs.\n2. Inside the encrypted file system, run `git clone https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim`. The clone fails due to a \"filename too long\" error.",
